Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/iptcutil/iptcutil.c
Line: 113
Function: formatString
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: iscntrl() is called with an int derived from a possibly signed char (*s). For bytes >= 0x80, c becomes negative and passing it to ctype functions is undefined behavior, which can index past the bounds of the ctype table. Cast to unsigned char before calling iscntrl.

